# This repo is PUBLIC and holds no code. Everything in it is meant to be read by
# strangers and by every installed copy of Job-I:
#
#   data/   the shipped JSON every install seeds and updates from. The source of truth -
#           edited in job-i-src and pushed here with `bun scripts/data.ts push`.
#   site/   the website, deployed to canyavall.github.io/job-i by .github/workflows/pages.yml.
#   manifest/  latest.json + .sig, written by the release and data-release workflows.
#
# So the rule here is the opposite of a normal .gitignore: nothing is excluded because it
# is generated, only because it has no business being public. A stray file in this repo is
# published, not just committed.

# Editor and Claude Code scratch.
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/temp/

# OS junk, which is how a folder listing ends up on a download page.
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# No tooling runs here (site/build.ts and the data scripts are plain Bun, no deps), so
# either of these appearing means something was installed by mistake.
node_modules/
bun.lock

# Belt and braces for the one thing that must never land in a public repo: the ed25519
# private key that signs manifest/latest.json. It lives in the JOBI_SIGNING_KEY secret on
# job-i-src and in the owner's password manager, and it is never written to a file here.
# Lose it and no installed copy can ever be updated again; leak it and anyone can ship
# code to all of them.
*.pem
*.key
*signing-key*

# A real CV or cover letter is never part of the site. The screenshots are webp/png.
*.docx
*.pdf
